{
  "_comment": [
    "Every non-CLI AI tool that deadreckon tracks: editors, agents, runtimes.",
    "",
    "This is an authored file: edit it by hand to add or remove programs.",
    "If this file does not exist, the system falls back to a built-in list",
    "hardcoded in sessions.py, so deleting it is always safe.",
    "",
    "Fields:",
    "  name              display name shown in reports",
    "  kind              'editor' | 'agent' | 'runtime'",
    "  paths             home-relative paths that prove the tool is installed",
    "  binary            command name checked with `which`, null if none",
    "  reader            key into sessions.READERS that counts this tool's tokens,",
    "                    null if no reader exists yet",
    "  store_labels      canonical stores.BY_LABEL entries read by reader; [] if none",
    "  no_tokens_because why this tool cannot be token-counted, null if it CAN be",
    "  tracks            what non-token metrics are tracked for this tool",
    "",
    "Why editors and agents are separate from CLIs:",
    "  CLIs are first-class token producers: they have readers, they write sessions,",
    "  they contribute to totals.json. Programs are tracked for presence, install",
    "  date, and usage patterns, but most cannot be token-counted because their",
    "  storage formats are undocumented or they host other agents' work."
  ],
  "programs": [
    {
      "name": "VS Code",
      "kind": "editor",
      "paths": [".config/Code"],
      "binary": "code",
      "reader": null,
      "no_tokens_because": "editor \u2014 hosts agents, spends no tokens itself",
      "tracks": ["install_date", "launches", "workspaces", "active_days"]
    },
    {
      "name": "VS Code Insiders",
      "kind": "editor",
      "paths": [".config/Code - Insiders"],
      "binary": "code-insiders",
